  "questions": [
    {
      "key": "1d2d5f1c-226f-4574-a859-d96eeb8ead0f",
      "id": "Q-01",
      "text": "With seven aircraft in the fly area at once, which aircraft does each camera detect, when and where, which observations are missed or false, and how often is an observation associated with the wrong aircraft?",
      "note": "Response per camera per aircraft: detection events with ground and slant range; missed observations; false detections; wrong associations. Vary: spacing (crossing pair at 5 m vertical, close pair at 16 m), speed (6 to 16 m/s), altitude (20 to 60 m AGL). Hold: camera settings as the ladder baseline. Record: sun, background, wind. Replicates: 2 runs minimum. Target-absent interval: 120 s before launch. Multi-aircraft association extends the single-aircraft method of the plan."
    }
  ],
